---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Developers"
  description="Developer access to Trackwise APIs. Sandbox and production access are gated by KYB and partner approval."
  eyebrow="Developers"
>
  <p>
    Trackwise APIs are exposed to onboarded customers. Public documentation
    and a sandbox are part of our roadmap. In the meantime, request early
    access through{' '}
    <a href="/contact">the contact form</a> (select <strong>Developer access</strong>).
  </p>

  <h2>API surface</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cards:</strong> create, freeze, replace, tokenize virtual and physical cards.</li>
    <li><strong>Accounts:</strong> open, list, close named beneficiary accounts (USD, EUR, GBP).</li>
    <li><strong>Ledger:</strong> double-entry primitives, balances, statements.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments:</strong> ACH, wire, SEPA, and partner remittance corridors.</li>
    <li><strong>Compliance:</strong> KYC / KYB orchestration, sanctions screening, case management.</li>
    <li><strong>Webhooks:</strong> signed, retried, idempotent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>
  <p>
    API access uses scoped API keys with optional IP allow-listing and HMAC
    request signing. All production credentials are issued after KYB and a
    written subscription agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Environments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sandbox:</strong> deterministic test data, full API surface, no real money movement.</li>
    <li><strong>Production:</strong> issued after KYB, integration review, and partner approval.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    A public status page is in progress. For incident communications, customers receive in-app
    notifications and email.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="/security">Security</a>. To report a vulnerability, email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:security@trackwise.finance">security@trackwise.finance</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
